    {
      "id": "claim_bec33f50b9d247c085dbc18587efe883",
      "statement": "LocalCache counts a modification only when put stores a new or different value; once the dirty counter exceeds MAX_DIRTY (50) it flushes automatically, flush() is an explicit write(), and write() is atomic — it writes <file>.tmp.json, copies over the target with REPLACE_EXISTING, deletes the temp file, and skips work entirely when nothing is dirty.",
